heck must carry an inline prose reason at the exempted site itself, not a silent entry in an external ignore list","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":[".Workflow/agent-workflows/shared/check-contract.ts:57"],"released":false},{"finding":"A gate's scope (what counts as reachable/covered) is computed by scanning the actual source-of-truth locations on every run, never maintained as a hand-written list, because a hand list drifts silently","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":["knip.config.ts:11"],"released":false},{"finding":"A template variable that could be empty is substituted with an explicit stated-absence sentence, never left to render as a hole","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":[".Workflow/agent-workflows/spec/critic.ts:40"],"released":false},{"finding":"Gate-enforcement logic reachable from multiple entry paths is factored into one shared function each path calls, rather than a rule each caller is independently trusted to follow","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":[".Workflow/agent-workflows/spec/spec.ts:258"],"released":false},{"finding":"A test proves a stage never ran by asserting the absence of that stage's unique distinguishing argument across every recorded call, rather than relying on call count alone","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":[".Workflow/agent-workflows/spec/spec.test.ts:174"],"released":false},{"finding":"**Zero-grandfather rails** — \"a new lint rule ships with no excused sites; the refactor lands first or in the same ticket... Red flag: a grandfather list, baseline file, or warn tier added alongside a new rule.\" This diff introduces the `wiring` check (`knip.config.ts`, wired into `bin/gauntlet push`) in the same commit range as a 31-entry baseline file that pre-excuses every standing violation. The stated exception is \"a genuinely large refactor, recorded on the ledger line with count and reason\" — but the baseline's own rationale describes 31 unrelated product decisions (\"wire the fixer, or delete it\") rather than one mechanical refactor, so the exception's shape doesn't match